-- Every blocked-call statistic filters on (action, timestamp): the three Home counters, the
-- seven-day chart, and the call-log screens. Without an index each is a full scan of a table
-- that only grows (nothing prunes it but the user's own "clear log"), so the cost climbs with
-- every call the app ever handles.
--
-- Named 1.sqm, not 2.sqm: a migration file N.sqm takes the schema from version N to
-- N+1, and the squashed baseline in databases/1.db is version 1. Numbering it 2 made
-- SQLDelight generate Schema.version = 3 with no migration for the 1 -> 2 step, so an
-- existing database jumped straight from 1 to 3 across a gap that does not exist.
--
-- Index-only migration: no table is rebuilt and no data moves, so this is safe to apply to a
-- populated database and needs none of the rename-copy-drop dance a CHECK-constraint change
-- would (see corta-spam-sqldelight-check-migration).
CREATE INDEX idx_call_log_action_time ON CallLogEntry(action, timestamp DESC);
